# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SeinARTS — project-wide .gitignore (monorepo: host project + all plugins)
# Bare directory patterns (no leading slash) match at ANY depth, so a single rule
# covers the project root AND every plugin (e.g. Plugins/*/Binaries/).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Unreal build / cache artifacts ──
Binaries/
Intermediate/
DerivedDataCache/
Saved/

# ── Plugin packaging output (PackagePlugins.ps1 → GitHub release zips) ──
/dist/

# ── Baked SeinARTS data (regenerable build artifacts — re-bake after clone) ──
# Level-data bakes are derived from level geometry + plugin code. After clone,
# open each level once and click "Bake Level Data" on the ASeinLevelVolume
# (unified pipeline, CP1.1 — saves to LevelDataSaveFolder, default /Game/LevelData).
# The NavData/FogOfWarData/Levels patterns are legacy (pre-CP1.1), kept for old clones.
# The **/ prefix is required so these match inside Plugins/.../Content, not just root.
**/Content/Levels/Data/
**/Content/NavData/
**/Content/FogOfWarData/
**/Content/LevelData/

# ── IDE / build tooling ──
.vs/
# .vscode/ is UE-regenerated with absolute paths; un-ignore if you keep custom tasks/launch
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sln
*.suo
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.vcxproj*
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/

# ── OS junk ──
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.DS_Store

# ── Python (UE editor scripting / tooling) ──
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Generated reports ──
# Requested PDFs belong in the user's Downloads directory, never in-tree.
/[Oo]utput/

# ── Claude Code local state (settings.local, worktrees, transcripts, etc.) ──
.claude/

# ── Local planning / design-doc scratch (nav/movement work — NOT code) ──
# Local working notes that re-ground future sessions; never committed to git.
planning/

# NOTE (tracked on purpose): *.uproject, *.uplugin, Config/, Source/, Content/
# (minus baked data above), Build.ps1, .vsconfig, and the per-plugin CLAUDE.md
# files are all version-controlled.
